<title>USA: U.S. Senator Lugar rules out wheat price hearings.</title>
<headline>U.S. Senator Lugar rules out wheat price hearings.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sen Richard Lugar, chairman of the Senate Agriculture Committee, Friday ruled out committee hearings on the drop in wheat prices.</p>
<p>In response to a question at the end of a foreign policy press conference, Lugar, Indiana Republican, said that if he held committee hearings whenever a commodity price dropped &quot;I would do nothing else.&quot;</p>
<p>There have been suggestions in Washington that the question of wheat prices should be examined at congressional hearings.</p>
<p>Lugar said that corn and soybean prices were also &quot;going down precipitously,&quot; noting that they were crops on his own farm.</p>
</text>
